  "summary": "Chapter17 now contains seven proofs for the restricted S10 geometry of canonical basic potentials on every diagonal Hopf manifold of dimension n>=3. The full Perron envelope descends to the projective base; basic finite-energy potentials have a complete CAT(0) metric and a unique metric-action-minimizing Perron segment. Smooth basic segments are stationary under every smooth variation, but constant translations have infinitely many negative raw-action directions and shorter nonbasic paths. Explicit diagonal geodesics, the sharp squared-energy exponent threshold and ordinary-model/Legendre pullback are included. The ordinary model projection of the entire basic finite-energy domain is zero, so general S10 remains open.",
